Well, Killashandra-S ascended about 10 minutes ago with about 4.5 million
points, spoilers & summary to follow after some linefeeds..





















Ok.  Well, the game started out quite well, since I found a set of crystal
plate mail on the first level, unfortunately, it was cursed, but it was +0
so I didn't particularly care and left it to sort out later.  Clearing out
the mines was pretty easy, unfortunately, I made the mistake of zapping
myself with a wand of make invisible in the beginning of the game, thus
making it impossible to enter shops. (until I got teleport that is)..

 Speaking of teleport, I picked up intristic teleport pretty soon after
that, which was a major nuisance until I reached castle level and wished
for a ring of teleport contrl (tengu's just weren't giving me tele-control
for some reason).  About level 5 or 6 my god gave me snickersee, and I
picked up excalibur shortly after that.  A Throne wish gave me GDSM, and
I picked up speedboots and Gauntlets of power inside the Castle.  After
wandering around hell for a while, I realized that I hadn't completed my
quest, so I backtracked up and finished it off, getting the Tsurgi and the
bell, then skipped across the the mines to pick up the luckstone that I
missed. Having maxed out the luck, and with an amulet of reflection, hell
wasn't all too hellish, with a good supply of holy water to keep
everything blessed.  Picked up the amulet, skipped back up, had lots of
K-rations to keep me going.  The trip up was really easy due to intristic
teleport and teleport control.  Made my way through the endgame, offered
the amulet, and bingo.

A few notes.. The quest was REALLY easy, unbelivably so.  By the time I
had reached second or so level of hell I had a complete set of
resistances, was very fast, extremelly lucky, extra luck, displaced,
protected, magic protected, etc. etc. etc.
 Also, wishes aren't what they used to be.  On finish I couldn't think of
much else to wish for (I had used 5) and I still had 3 in wand and a magic
lamp.  (3 used from the wand, one other lamp, and a throne)

Oh well, back to hack.

